Subject: [PATCH] gbp_agent: drop eventlet monkey-patch for OpenStack 2026.1

neutron removed eventlet in the 2026.1 cycle. Both the
``neutron.common.eventlet_utils`` module and the whole
``neutron/cmd/eventlet/`` package (whose ``__init__.py`` contained exactly
these two statements) were deleted, so the import at the top of
gbp_agent.py aborts neutron-opflex-agent at startup with:

    ImportError: cannot import name 'eventlet_utils' from 'neutron.common'

``eventlet_utils.monkey_patch()`` was a pure side-effecting call (it ran
``eventlet.monkey_patch()`` plus a pyroute2 asyncio fixup and returned
None); ``eventlet_utils`` is not referenced anywhere else in this file, so
removing both lines is sufficient and complete.

Re-adding a bare ``import eventlet; eventlet.monkey_patch()`` would be
wrong: neutron 2026.1 is designed to run un-patched on native threads, and
neutron's own OVS agent entry point -- the class GBPOpflexAgent subclasses
-- no longer monkey-patches at all.

Applied against the installed copy in the venv, because the opflex-agent
Dockerfile runs kolla_patch after `pip install /opflex-agent`.
Path uses the version-independent `python3` symlink created in
docker/openstack-base/Dockerfile.j2.

--- var/lib/kolla/venv/lib/python3/site-packages/opflexagent/gbp_agent.py
+++ var/lib/kolla/venv/lib/python3/site-packages/opflexagent/gbp_agent.py
@@ -15,11 +15,6 @@
 import sys
 import time

-# We need to ensure that the monkey-patch gets applied
-# before other packages that use eventlet get imported
-from neutron.common import eventlet_utils  # noqa
-eventlet_utils.monkey_patch()  # noqa
-
 from neutron.agent.common import ip_lib
 from neutron.agent.common import polling
 from neutron.agent import rpc as agent_rpc
